faqs:
  - q: "Should we use round-robin assignment in HubSpot?"
    a: "Use round-robin as the last rule, not the first. Territory, named-account, product, and language rules should decide ownership first. Round-robin then spreads the remaining leads across reps who have capacity and are not out of office."
  - q: "What happens to leads when a rep is on leave?"
    a: "Routing should skip unavailable reps and assign to a named fallback owner or team queue. Existing open leads owned by the absent rep should be reassigned or watched by a manager until they return, so SLA timers keep working."
  - q: "How fast should new leads be contacted?"
    a: "Set the response target by lead type and priority, agree it with sales leadership, and measure it. A demo request usually deserves a faster target than a content download. What matters most is that the target is written down, timed in HubSpot, and escalated when missed."
